# CHANGELOG.md is generated from changelog.d/ by tools/compile-changelog.ts
# and staged by the pre-commit hook. Marking it generated collapses it in
# GitHub diffs, where it is noise rather than review material.
#
# Deliberately NOT given a custom merge driver: a driver that regenerates the
# file runs before git has placed the other side's new fragment in the working
# tree, so it silently rebuilds from incomplete input and drops entries. On a
# conflict here, run `pnpm changelog:compile` and stage the result instead.
CHANGELOG.md linguist-generated=true
